<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Charles O'Hara</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1740–1802</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Charles O'Hara was a British army officer who served as governor of the Province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/senegambia">Senegambia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>'s colony on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/senegal">Senegal</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/the-gambia">Gambia</a> rivers, from 1765 to 1776, where he was accused of harsh rule and slave trading. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-revolutionary-war">American Revolutionary War</a> he surrendered the British army at Yorktown in 1781 for Cornwallis. He later governed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gibraltar">Gibraltar</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/charles-ohara.jpg" alt="Charles O'Hara" width="320" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lieutenant-General_Charles_O%27Hara.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
